      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "GENUINE LADY (4) made it a double here from 3 starts last month when scoring comfortably by a length over 1200m 12 days ago, following on from a brave all-the-way win by a nose over the same trip. She tries a mile for the first time, and will take plenty of catching. The hat-trick beckons. THICKSKINNED (3) drops down in class after finishing fifth here over 1600m 12 days ago. His win carrying 59kg at the start before is the guide to use, and he can make amends, especially with Darmanin returning to the saddle. Stick with him. LAST TREMBLE (6) was a month between starts when dropping back to 1400m and peaking late to finish seventh. She is better placed over 1600m, and with only 8 days since that most recent effort, she should be kept very safe. Value. SIR JAG (2) was only just over a length from the winner when finishing third at Hobart last start, and he is always a top 4 threat. LITTLE EL (7) won over 2000m here 2 starts back, then was second last start over this trip. Include.",
